{:db/id 17592186119888 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186119708 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Parametric Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "1b4b69f7-fc4f-57c3-bcaf-9df98e4fc5e3" :question/math-academy-id "e-8947" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx = u, \\quad \ny = v, \\quad \nz = 1 - u - v\n$$\n\nfor $-1 \\leq u \\leq 1$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 3.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r (u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\,\\textrm d S = \\iint\\limits_D  \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u, \\: v, \\: 1 - u - v \\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand its magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD = \\{ (u,v) \\: : \\: -1 \\leq u \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq v \\leq 3\\}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\text{ }\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186050207} {:db/id 17592186050546}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186120078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Parametric Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bfe5eea-2ed5-57d1-920c-5bf7749bd52c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{70}" :db/id 17592186238163} {:answer/id #uuid "28eb82e3-6a9c-5de4-9c73-f476cef15973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id 17592186238416} {:answer/id #uuid "44d82293-ae28-5a3b-91f7-6f335e4e5f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{30}" :db/id 17592186238652} {:answer/id #uuid "5574b951-f5f1-5ffb-80db-fad8029179eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id 17592186238793} {:answer/id #uuid "e1123ef7-3b43-5120-a22c-5cde4bfdb285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{35}" :db/id 17592186240030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bfe5eea-2ed5-57d1-920c-5bf7749bd52c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{70}" :db/id 17592186238163} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc9f1b5d-bcf1-568c-bbaf-58ab6b82ef80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186240772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04aeca54-3b07-58c4-888a-6b39f758095a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105920" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=2u-v,\\,y=3u+2,\\,z=u+2v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $-1\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u-v,\\,3u+2,\\,u+2v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u+2),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,3,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u+2),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,-5,\\,3⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨6,\\,-5,\\,3⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+25+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{70}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}{∬}_{D}\\text{ }\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}\\cdot 1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186120079 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Parametric Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "411bf46a-dda1-51f0-bd59-b820659afb72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi \\sqrt{57}" :db/id 17592186238619} {:answer/id #uuid "6900a7b8-7d5a-562e-9c9d-ad769c178da7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{19}" :db/id 17592186238966} {:answer/id #uuid "83aef3ae-1313-5321-a641-f9fa2ba69ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi \\sqrt{19}" :db/id 17592186239202} {:answer/id #uuid "87703ec0-9ddc-5d7d-a758-6baa7dc46d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{38}" :db/id 17592186239232} {:answer/id #uuid "d7def3e5-8bf5-5eb5-99c2-b1acdcaf5acf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi \\sqrt{38}" :db/id 17592186239937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83aef3ae-1313-5321-a641-f9fa2ba69ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi \\sqrt{19}" :db/id 17592186239202} :answer-field/id #uuid "accfc2a2-378a-5435-9ff9-d8a31a34f2e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186240634}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fae50a6d-3a64-5292-bf93-f5341ecb7d4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105922" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨-u+v,\\,u-2v,\\,3v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 4.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,3,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨3,\\,3,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 4$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 4},\n$$\n\nof radius $2.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{19}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\pi \\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186247030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Parametric Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39ee8c68-1864-57de-a946-4d5491f72162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{10}" :db/id 17592186244826} {:answer/id #uuid "3c6058cd-ef3c-5b04-9408-d57007317bbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186244843} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2a11de-f795-5b2e-9701-89f49ea4e8e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{22}" :db/id 17592186245018} {:answer/id #uuid "55f22ff4-a11d-5608-9228-8c9c4e21d127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{14}" :db/id 17592186245070} {:answer/id #uuid "af8101ed-0f01-5edf-b92b-9155125b12fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{11}" :db/id 17592186245881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f2a11de-f795-5b2e-9701-89f49ea4e8e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{22}" :db/id 17592186245018} :answer-field/id #uuid "97488496-77bc-5262-b42c-1231cd7a5226" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186246811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "84f10468-a9ec-54bf-a4d6-59a03d61dbaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-109710" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y=2-3u,\\,z=1+u-v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $-1\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,2-3u,\\,1+u-v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2-3u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-3,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2-3u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,2,\\,3⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨3,\\,2,\\,3⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186247031 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Parametric Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a511b6f-0600-5198-a79a-e5527e8f7af1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id 17592186244549} {:answer/id #uuid "781bc53d-6da8-596b-92ef-3b236df69123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id 17592186245380} {:answer/id #uuid "97a2dde0-64ef-5072-b3c5-71c64fc80cee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id 17592186245651} {:answer/id #uuid "cfbef9b2-a6dc-5bfa-ae03-27e59b80192b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{6}" :db/id 17592186246168} {:answer/id #uuid "f925caff-0904-5fa2-afc1-5cc9e4eb7a19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id 17592186246505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a511b6f-0600-5198-a79a-e5527e8f7af1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id 17592186244549} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b2a4171-2411-5190-8229-ee37e0db2e69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186246568}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d492e8b2-2ae8-555e-8788-3c26b7ebc400" :question/math-academy-id "q-109712" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y={v}^{2},\\,z=\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\sqrt{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,2{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 2{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2v & 2{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2{v}^{2},\\,2v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨0,\\,-2{v}^{2},\\,2v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2{v}^{2})^{2}+(2v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{4}+4{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}({v}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{v}^{2}}=v$ since $v\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le \\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the substitution \n\n$$\nw={v}^{2}+1\\,⇒\\,\\text{d}w=2v\\,\\text{d}v,\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{w}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{w}^{3}}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\sqrt{{4}^{3}}-\\sqrt{{1}^{3}}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186247040 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Parametric Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81df853c-c7b7-503a-81f4-854a8d9dd531" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id 17592186245462} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a7eecb-208c-5bb4-b7a1-8c9244d1069f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186245822} {:answer/id #uuid "e86c003f-fdb5-59bd-8dc8-507c0b72a262" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id 17592186246370} {:answer/id #uuid "f8b0d156-8308-5819-9741-f9503e77ca41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id 17592186246503} {:answer/id #uuid "fdfd09ae-23c2-518b-a998-39c77888edd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id 17592186246535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8a7eecb-208c-5bb4-b7a1-8c9244d1069f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186245822} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd5766b3-0604-500f-bffc-f2b07efa78de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186246941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c206356-09e7-589f-8fd6-4bbad41aebab" :question/math-academy-id "q-109761" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y=uv,\\,z=\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $1\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,uv,\\,\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,v,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,u,\\,v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & v & 0 \\\\ 0 & u & v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}v & 0 \\\\ u & v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{v}^{2},\\,-2uv,\\,2{u}^{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨{v}^{2},\\,-2uv,\\,2{u}^{2}⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({v}^{2})^{2}+(-2uv)^{2}+(2{u}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{v}^{4}+4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+4{u}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({v}^{2}+2{u}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & ={v}^{2}+2{u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,1\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({v}^{2}+2{u}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({v}^{2}+2{u}^{2})\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[u{v}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3}]}_{0}^{1}\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}({v}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3})\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}+\\frac{2}{3}v]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[{2}^{3}+2(2)-({1}^{3}+2(1))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(9) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186247046 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Parametric Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a2e4bdd-442c-5db5-9f63-c23adc2689fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id 17592186244690} {:answer/id #uuid "49dc1ed9-4cad-5a2c-8301-d22f556db3cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{3}" :db/id 17592186244971} {:answer/id #uuid "6621db82-2238-537b-9c86-6e6889b3eb73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\pi \\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186245213} {:answer/id #uuid "7060d728-881c-574f-9bb2-5498f2a3deb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\pi \\sqrt{3}" :db/id 17592186245320} {:answer/id #uuid "8b4ca8a3-27e9-57c9-af53-8832d20f6d9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186245537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7060d728-881c-574f-9bb2-5498f2a3deb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\pi \\sqrt{3}" :db/id 17592186245320} :answer-field/id #uuid "15dadaf4-eeb3-594f-bfbb-198fd6c49858" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186246585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "41677fe6-6daf-5332-9eef-d0840faca5fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-109779" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 9.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 9$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 9},\n$$\n\nof radius $3.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\\pi \\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186247100 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Parametric Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "025f0489-87f5-5a9f-add3-b7a1173218b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{20}" :db/id 17592186244328} {:answer/id #uuid "091b32cf-3a1d-5b7c-bdc7-3d5f6a69cd98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi \\sqrt{10}" :db/id 17592186244389} {:answer/id #uuid "5b48dc53-794d-5288-8722-cc17c2171077" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi \\sqrt{5}" :db/id 17592186245113} {:answer/id #uuid "a9c5345d-feb7-5bcf-a354-6148292fa771" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{15}" :db/id 17592186245829} {:answer/id #uuid "f3113b15-3a1a-584d-913c-08a25612137a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi \\sqrt{30}" :db/id 17592186246461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3113b15-3a1a-584d-913c-08a25612137a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi \\sqrt{30}" :db/id 17592186246461} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e01c6e8-5c98-5791-a262-2b4a7162b8c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186246772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "266cc575-6c30-52b6-9198-190d4fbe9593" :question/math-academy-id "q-110252" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,1-2u+5v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-2u+5v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-2u+5v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,-5,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨2,\\,-5,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{(-5)}^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+25+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 2$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 2}\n$$\n\nof radius $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{30}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot (\\sqrt{2})^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\sqrt{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186247141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9361ad5a-b15c-507b-85d4-fe7ccb4d9fd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Parametric Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ab3c21a-7901-5e8a-b919-8ac158d0b3ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{17}" :db/id 17592186244832} {:answer/id #uuid "4a1afc8b-e18c-59b0-8629-409f8bad9d56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{35}" :db/id 17592186244973} {:answer/id #uuid "7e300a0f-c019-5688-aa90-d9d3c280a735" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{15}" :db/id 17592186245430} {:answer/id #uuid "94156068-3295-59c4-b393-88ea63372de6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi \\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186245608} {:answer/id #uuid "c23438eb-159b-5522-8561-54d501b4334c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi \\sqrt{11}" :db/id 17592186246047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a1afc8b-e18c-59b0-8629-409f8bad9d56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{35}" :db/id 17592186244973} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a678cbb-8af1-5c41-a2b0-0bb51a36b874" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186246669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3426a71b-5b0e-56f2-83bf-dae50aa51435" :question/math-academy-id "q-110551" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,u+2v,\\,2u-v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,\\,-1,\\,3⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-5,\\,-1,\\,3⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+1+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 1$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 1},\n$$\n\nof radius $1.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{35}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\pi \\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Parametric Surface"}